    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABJksxOQ",
      "title": "lagoon: specify that the block gas limit bounds pre-refund gas under SDM",
      "author": "geoknee",
      "number": 974,
      "body": "SDM implementations already enforce the block gas limit against pre-refund gas, but the Lagoon specs never state it. This PR writes the rule down.\n\nThe rule is consensus-relevant. A client built from the spec could reasonably check the limit against canonical (post-refund) gas, which would admit more execution per block than op-reth and Kona accept, and the chain would split.\n\n## Change\n\n`sdm.md` gets a new **Block Gas Limit** subsection under Canonical Gas. Before executing transaction `i`, a verifier MUST check\n\n```text\ngasLimit(i) <= blockGasLimit - sum(evmGasUsed(j) for j < i)\n```\n\nA transaction that fails the check invalidates the block. This implies the usual check against canonical `gasUsed`, and is identical to it when a block carries no refunds.\n\nIt also adds a matching **Block resource limit** entry to Security Considerations. The entry notes that the EIP-7623 floor's resource bound survives SDM, because the floor is part of `evmGasUsed`.\n\n## Implementation reference\n\n`OpBlockExecutor::execute_transaction_without_commit` in [`rust/alloy-op-evm/src/block/mod.rs`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/ca63e7ee6fbb23b4f8b6ef97e7a5921e2ec4346a/rust/alloy-op-evm/src/block/mod.rs#L1039-L1047) does the check by passing `blockGasLimit - evm_gas_used` to `validate_block_gas`. op-reth and the Kona executor share this code.\n\nFound during the SDM FMA finalization review (FM3).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-20T14:39:33Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-20T15:45:58Z",
